<!--
    Two functions touch one 8-byte global no symbol names: store64 writes all
    of it, load_high reads its upper 4 bytes. Upstream Funcdata::mapGlobals
    adds a DAT_ Symbol for the 8-byte group to the global scope while it
    decompiles store64, so a load_high decompiled after it in the same session
    reads a piece of that Symbol. Kuna recorded nothing (its per-function
    GlobalQuery is a snapshot no action can write), so load_high always read a
    free-standing dat_105004. The same holds for the coverVarnodes names:
    read_wide reads 8 bytes at the int4 `small` and 4 at small+4, and mapGlobals names that upper half
    small_4, and read_upper, decompiled next, reads that half alone.

    Stage model: P9 emit, naming-policy (p9_emit/coreaction_render.rs
    map_globals records the group; p9_emit/kuna_mapglobalsyms.rs persist adds
    it to the global scope after the function).

    Option: mapglobalsyms (default off). Pass 1 is off, pass 2 on; the same
    two functions are decompiled in the same order in both.
-->
